      "summary": "The JWT matcher does not implement the specified shape-only recognition rule, and the tests do not cover the required non-`e` header case.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Diagnostics/RedactionFilter.cs",
          "line": 23,
          "message": "JWT redaction misses the required shape when the first segment does not start with `e`, allowing tokens into telemetry.",
          "confidence": 0.99,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "Log properties, scopes, trace tags, and event attributes pass string values through Sanitize to ScrubText, where Jwt() matches JWT-like values only when the first segment starts with `ew` or `ey`.",
            "failureScenario": "A caller logs `YWJjZGVm.abcdefgh.ijklmnop` under an ordinary property name. Its three base64url segments are each at least eight characters, but the first starts with `Y`, so the regex leaves the value unchanged and it reaches the log provider. The required regression test for a header starting with a character other than `e` is also absent. OWASP A09:2025."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "agentId": "test-reviewer-codex",
